# The original, from the Monroe Institute of Applied Sciences Gateway
# Intermediate Workbook (1977) -- the CIA FOIA release. Longer than the settled
# form: "to those who follow me" rather than "near and close to me", and a
# closing protection clause the other forms leave out.
#
# Offered, not prescribed. Protection here is a thing you may want, not a thing
# the exercise requires.

@segment   affirmation-1977
@title     The Gateway Affirmation — 1977 original
@levels    F10
@family    affirmation
@fixed
@duration  ~1m30s

say Say in your mind. Say to yourself.
pause 4
say I am more than my physical body. Because I am more than physical matter, I can perceive that which is greater than the physical world.
pause 6
say Therefore, in these exercises, I deeply desire to expand, to experience, to know, to understand, to control, to use such greater energies and energy systems as may be beneficial and constructive to me, and to those who follow me.
pause 8
say Also during these exercises, I deeply desire the help and cooperation, the assistance, the understanding, of those individuals whose wisdom, development, and experience are equal or greater than my own.
pause 8
say I ask their guidance and protection from any influence or any source that might provide me with less than my stated desires.
pause 6
say I now protect myself as may be needed from such influence, and reject any source that may restrain me from my stated desires.
pause 10
